   737	      # ==========================================================
   738	      # PLAN-166 W1-B — verdict delta + ancestry gate (F2 server side)
   739	      # ==========================================================
   740	      # Re-pass findings r15 + r17 + r18 (PLAN-166), debate r3 scoped VETO.
   741	      #
   742	      # WHY A SEPARATE STEP: the step-15 neighbourhood above carries two
   743	      # escape hatches keyed to CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL —
   744	      # `continue-on-error:` on the step itself, and an empty
   745	      # `--parent-sha ""` bind (the validator only binds the field when
   746	      # args.parent_sha is non-empty). Inheriting that neighbourhood would
   747	      # inherit the switch. This step therefore:
   748	      #   - carries NO continue-on-error;
   749	      #   - FAILS CLOSED when CEO_PAIR_RAIL_VERDICT_OPTIONAL=1: in that
   750	      #     mode step 15 skipped the parent_sha bind, so the anchor these
   751	      #     asserts hang off was never validated — there is no transition
   752	      #     mode here, by design;
   753	      #   - re-derives and re-binds parent_sha ITSELF (non-empty, 40-hex,
   754	      #     equal to the verdict's `parent_sha:` read with the SAME parser
   755	      #     the local tag guard uses) — independent of step 15's outcome,
   756	      #     which also closes the legacy commit_sha fallback (the
